--TEST--
The shapes of the worked program `nvs agent primer` prints answer what its comments say: the options bag orders the strings, and a string that is not an integer throws a `RuntimeError` at `as int` that a `catch` sees, where `as ?int` answers `null` — `rule:tooling/a-primer-claim-is-executed`, `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:expressions/nullable-conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:agents/nvs-agent-primer
// The shapes of the primer's worked program, then the claims its comments make
// that the output the primer prints beside it does not show.

array<string> $amounts = ["3", "11", "7"];
array<string> $ordered = Core\Arr::sort($amounts, {order: Core\Order::Asc});

int $total = 0;
foreach ($ordered as string $each) {
    $total = $total + ($each as int);
}
echo Core\Json::encode($ordered), " ", $total, "\n";

// The bag is what orders the strings: the other case reverses them.
echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Arr::sort($amounts, {order: Core\Order::Desc})), "\n";

// "a string that is not an integer throws", once per string, and a `catch`
// sees each one. `as ?int` is the conversion that answers `null` instead.
array<string> $refused = ["seven", "7.0", " 7", ""];
foreach ($refused as string $text) {
    try {
        int $value = $text as int;
        echo $value, "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $thrown) {
        echo $thrown->message, "\n";
    }
    ?int $maybe = $text as ?int;
    echo $maybe == null ? "null" : "an int", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
["11","3","7"] 21
["7","3","11"]
cannot convert string "seven" to `int`
null
cannot convert string "7.0" to `int`
null
cannot convert string " 7" to `int`
null
cannot convert string "" to `int`
null
